# VPN Worker Pool — /opt/load-balancer/workers.conf
# Format: hostname:port  (one per line, # for comments, blank lines ignored)
#
# The collector script reads this file every 60 seconds and polls each
# worker's load agent at http://<hostname>:<port>/
#
# IMPORTANT — DNS resolution notes:
#   These hostnames must resolve to the worker's DIRECT PUBLIC IP.
#   Do NOT use Cloudflare-proxied hostnames (orange cloud) — Cloudflare
#   doesn't proxy port 9099. Create a separate A record with grey cloud
#   (DNS only) or use raw IP addresses.
#
#   Example DNS setup:
#     worker-a.yourdomain.com  →  A  1.2.3.4   (grey cloud, DNS only)
#     worker-b.yourdomain.com  →  A  5.6.7.8   (grey cloud, DNS only)
#
# The last line (127.0.0.1:9099) polls the orchestrator itself.
# This ensures the orchestrator considers its own load when deciding
# where to place new clients. The orchestrator also runs all VPN
# protocols and handles its own share of traffic.

# ---- Active Workers ----

vps-a.yourdomain.com:9099
vps-b.yourdomain.com:9099
# vps-c.yourdomain.com:9099   (temporarily removed for maintenance)

127.0.0.1:9099
